// A2 course (A1 → A2 roadmap), module 14 „Õppimine, kool ja keel” (a2-066…070), level A2, in the final shape
// (docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_A2.md, row m14 = m6: RÄÄK LUGE PROJ KIRJ, with the leads of modules 11–19; gates
// V1–V16 of docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_B1.md §8). One storyline, one year before the B1 course (docs/COURSE_CAST.md): May. The spring course at
// Keelekool Sõna (teacher Maret, administrator Ene) ends on Friday 28 May; the last test is on Friday 21 May. Students Sofia, Tom, Lucía,
// Dmitri and Olga choose a summer course (from 7 June). Lucía says „jah” when she has not understood; Tom misses a lesson. The new teacher
// Aune helps them with the study card (the module product) and the two-week plan (31 May – 13 June). Pictures of the Kasuta sheets
// (art/visuals/a2-module-14.js): 068 Sofia and Aune at the study plan, 070 Aune's cards.
//   066 RÄÄK R→S  the course and the timetable: kursusel / kursusele / kursuselt, tunnis / tundi / tunnist, esmaspäeviti, kaks korda
//                 nädalas; corner S2 (one asks, the other answers, S05); main: the learner talks about the course (S02).
//   067 LUGE R→W  asking for help: korda / korrake, rääkige aeglasemalt, Mida see sõna tähendab?, Kas te saate …?; corner R4 (a text on
//                 Maret's Italian); main: a 50–70-word letter to the teacher (W08).
//   068 PROJ L→S  the study card: tahan / proovin + da, hakkan + ma; corner L4 (a talk on personal life, matching); main: the pair agrees
//                 on the cards (S03); home recording: the picture (S06).
//   069 KIRJ L→W  the two-week plan: iga päev, kaks korda nädalas, igal õhtul, pean / hakkan + ma; corner W1 (a text from a business card);
//                 main: a 60–80-word plan (W05), planned and edited.
//   070 EKS       the module exam, every part timed (B.examPart); tasks tagged R1–R5, L1–L4, W1, W2a, W2b, S0, S1, S2.
// Every teaching lesson: „Mäletad?” naming the previous lesson and one of modules 11–12, an in-lesson pair task, a home recording in
// Kasuta, two fluency tasks, one exam corner. No tingiv kõneviis (A2): „Kas te saate …?”, never „Kas te saaksite …?”.
